[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59493,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma is a rare, benign myxoid soft tissue tumour morphologically similar to intramuscular/cellular myxoma (but lacking <em>GNAS</em> mutation), typically arising in the vicinity of large joints.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59494,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8840/0 Myxoma NOS</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T09:39:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59495,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>2E84.Z &amp; XH6Q84 Benign fibrogenic or myofibrogenic tumour, site unknown &amp; Myxoma NOS</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T17:11:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59496,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> periarticular myxoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59497,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59498,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Juxta-articular myxoma usually arises adjacent to large joints, with the knee joint being the most commonly affected site (&gt;&nbsp;85%). Other locations affected are the shoulder, elbow, hip, and ankle {1592386}, and rare locations include the temporomandibular joint {26594976}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59499,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a swelling or a mass that may be associated with tenderness or pain in the vicinity of large joints. Duration of symptoms ranges from weeks to years. Imaging studies are similar to those of intramuscular myxoma {7747183}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59500,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These lesions occur over a wide age range, including rarely in children, but they typically affect patients in the fifth and sixth decades of life, with a male predominance {1592386}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59501,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In most patients, the etiology is unknown. A minority of patients have a history of trauma or osteoarthritis, which may be coincidental.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59502,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59503,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour usually ranges in size between 2 and 6&nbsp;cm, but tumours as large as 13&nbsp;cm have been described {1592386}. The cut surface is gelatinous and myxoid. Cystic degeneration is commonly seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59504,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is generally hypocellular and composed of bland spindle-shaped cells with uniform ovoid nuclei, inconspicuous nuclei, and palely eosinophilic cytoplasm embedded in a hypovascular myxoid stroma. Increased cellularity can be seen (similar to in cellular myxoma); however, mitoses are scarce. In the majority of cases, cyst-like spaces lined by a delicate fibrin layer or a thicker layer composed of collagen may be seen. The tumour is poorly circumscribed, demonstrating infiltration into the surrounding adipose or tendinous tissue. In a subset of cases, haemorrhage, chronic inflammation, and haemosiderin/fibrin deposition may be seen, probably due to trauma. These reactive changes may also be seen in recurrent tumours. Immunohistochemically, the lesional cells may express CD34 and/or SMA. S100 is negative. CD163-positive muciphages may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59505,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59506,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unlike intramuscular myxomas, juxta-articular myxomas do not demonstrate <em>GNAS</em> mutations {11942570}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59507,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> affects soft tissue around large joints, most commonly the knee (&gt;&nbsp;85%); hypocellular myxoid cytologically bland tumour; infiltrative growth pattern.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> lacks <em>GNAS</em> mutations (in selected cases).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59508,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 59509,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrence occurs in as many as one&nbsp;third of patients, sometimes more than once {1592386}. Malignant transformation does not occur.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-17T14:41:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]